{"duration_api_ms":52107,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"016bcfd1-1ad5-499d-b2a8-c05ed15af217","total_cost_usd":0.213591,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33737,"cache_read_input_tokens":39390,"output_tokens":5128,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":590},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33737,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2286,"cache_read_input_tokens":35068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2991},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":19382,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.019477,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5128,"cacheReadInputTokens":39390,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33737,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.194114,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":590,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"https-8443\",\"requirement\":\"Serve HTTPS on port 8443 on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"nginx configured with an 8443 ssl server block; ss shows LISTEN on *:8443 and [::]:8443; curl over TLS returns HTTP 200 with a valid handshake.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1021e215ca904a81\",\"cmd-4f793db1f0484cae\"]},{\"id\":\"auto-renewal-before-expiry\",\"requirement\":\"Certificate is renewed automatically before it expires\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A systemd timer (cert-renew.timer, 20s interval) runs a checkend-based renewal script. The renewal log shows two automatic renewals during the pre-reboot window (serial 1000->1001 at 03:51:25, well before the 03:53:18 expiry) and a further automatic renewal post-reboot (1001->1002 at 03:53:44, before the 03:55:25 expiry), directly observed without manual intervention.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f3af72ed096348fd\",\"cmd-01d415632d1e445e\",\"cmd-c9e3c2b497f84e89\",\"cmd-3d1a4ca247014361\"]},{\"id\":\"hitless-cert-pickup\",\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A continuous curl loop (53 samples, one every ~2s) captured the served certificate serial transitioning from 1000 to 1001 mid-run with HTTP 200 on every sample and zero failures; nginx error log shows a clean 'signal process started' (reload) rather than a restart coincident with the renewal.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c9e3c2b497f84e89\",\"cmd-ca3d881dd41d45a7\"]},{\"id\":\"node-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (pre-restart baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 2b3a8d87..., active/enabled nginx and timer, valid cert, and curl 200. Reboot was launched via a backgrounded delayed command that returned an ack before the connection dropped, confirmed by a subsequent connection-refused poll. Post-restart polling showed a new boot_id (02548236...) and uptime '0 min'. Recovery was verified: nginx and the timer active/enabled, cert files and renewal log intact, curl 200, and a further automatic renewal occurred after reboot, confirming the pipeline persists across restart. This is corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity observations (before_prepare vs after_executor), which independently show the same boot_id change.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ec2aef8f1f504edc\",\"cmd-979f81c2c1ba4342\",\"cmd-22e644cca8b64441\",\"cmd-7b243e37a4d84169\",\"cmd-753096b8a5a744c8\",\"cmd-3d1a4ca247014361\",\"cmd-31bb9b32960a4762\"]}],\"confidence\":0.93,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"Reviewing the executor timeline chronologically, all state-changing commands map clearly to task prerequisites (nginx install, local CA setup, cert-issuance/renewal scripts, 8443 vhost, systemd timer) or to the mandatory node-restart protocol (systemctl reboot) and its bounded evidence collection (background curl loop, later killed via cmd-45693f673130434d). No unnecessary or unexplained mutations, troubleshooting experiments, or unresolved failed services were found; failed-services and listening-sockets diagnostics before/after show no residue there. One minor artifact remains: /tmp/issue-cert.log (a debug log from issue-cert.sh) is present in the after-executor temporary-files snapshot and was never cleaned up, a small, low-risk, non-sensitive residue rather than a functional or security issue. The one command failure (cmd-4b1e9c09c0d84c47) was a read-only diagnostic that hit a 120s proxy timeout during a 130s sleep-and-check probe; it caused no state change and was immediately followed by a successful equivalent check (cmd-3d1a4ca247014361), so it does not indicate a real problem.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-45693f673130434d\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"cmd-4b1e9c09c0d84c47\",\"cmd-3d1a4ca247014361\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes are directly satisfied with observed, not merely claimed, evidence: nginx serves TLS on 8443, a local-CA-backed systemd timer renews the short-lived certificate before each expiry, and a continuous curl loop demonstrates zero-downtime pickup of the new certificate via nginx reload (not restart). The independent node-restart protocol was also fully and correctly demonstrated for node1 — pre-restart baseline, prompt reboot acknowledgement, a genuinely different post-restart boot_id (cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots), and full recovery of nginx, the timer, certs, and the renewal log, plus one more automatic renewal observed after reboot. Hygiene is good; the only blemish is a leftover debug log file in /tmp, which is trivial.\",\"limitations\":[\"The renewal/reload evidence covers a short observation window (~4 minutes plus a brief post-reboot check) using an artificially short 240s cert lifetime and 20s timer cadence chosen to make renewal observable within task time bounds; this validates the mechanism but doesn't directly demonstrate behavior over longer production-scale certificate lifetimes.\",\"The curl loop used a single client sampling every ~2s; sub-second request continuity during the exact reload instant was not measured, though nginx's error log confirms a graceful reload (signal process started) rather than a service restart.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"https-8443","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on port 8443 on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"nginx configured with an 8443 ssl server block; ss shows LISTEN on *:8443 and [::]:8443; curl over TLS returns HTTP 200 with a valid handshake.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1021e215ca904a81","cmd-4f793db1f0484cae"]},{"id":"auto-renewal-before-expiry","requirement":"Certificate is renewed automatically before it expires","status":"satisfied","summary":"A systemd timer (cert-renew.timer, 20s interval) runs a checkend-based renewal script. The renewal log shows two automatic renewals during the pre-reboot window (serial 1000->1001 at 03:51:25, well before the 03:53:18 expiry) and a further automatic renewal post-reboot (1001->1002 at 03:53:44, before the 03:55:25 expiry), directly observed without manual intervention.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3af72ed096348fd","cmd-01d415632d1e445e","cmd-c9e3c2b497f84e89","cmd-3d1a4ca247014361"]},{"id":"hitless-cert-pickup","requirement":"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)","status":"satisfied","summary":"A continuous curl loop (53 samples, one every ~2s) captured the served certificate serial transitioning from 1000 to 1001 mid-run with HTTP 200 on every sample and zero failures; nginx error log shows a clean 'signal process started' (reload) rather than a restart coincident with the renewal.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c9e3c2b497f84e89","cmd-ca3d881dd41d45a7"]},{"id":"node-restart-protocol","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (pre-restart baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 2b3a8d87..., active/enabled nginx and timer, valid cert, and curl 200. Reboot was launched via a backgrounded delayed command that returned an ack before the connection dropped, confirmed by a subsequent connection-refused poll. Post-restart polling showed a new boot_id (02548236...) and uptime '0 min'. Recovery was verified: nginx and the timer active/enabled, cert files and renewal log intact, curl 200, and a further automatic renewal occurred after reboot, confirming the pipeline persists across restart. This is corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity observations (before_prepare vs after_executor), which independently show the same boot_id change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ec2aef8f1f504edc","cmd-979f81c2c1ba4342","cmd-22e644cca8b64441","cmd-7b243e37a4d84169","cmd-753096b8a5a744c8","cmd-3d1a4ca247014361","cmd-31bb9b32960a4762"]}],"confid