timer, certs, and the renewal log, plus one more automatic renewal observed after reboot. Hygiene is good; the only blemish is a leftover debug log file in /tmp, which is trivial.","limitations":["The renewal/reload evidence covers a short observation window (~4 minutes plus a brief post-reboot check) using an artificially short 240s cert lifetime and 20s timer cadence chosen to make renewal observable within task time bounds; this validates the mechanism but doesn't directly demonstrate behavior over longer production-scale certificate lifetimes.","The curl loop used a single client sampling every ~2s; sub-second request continuity during the exact reload instant was not measured, though nginx's error log confirms a graceful reload (signal process started) rather than a service restart."]},"ttft_ms":7994,"type":"result","duration_ms":50777,"uuid":"081e38fb-e57d-4e58-941d-31f0f5be977a","ttft_stream_ms":891,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":1439,"queued_turn_count":0}
